{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.BringFiberActionInstance","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.BringFiberActionInstance","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.S5SO3FiberAction","lean:module:Mathlib.Analysis.SpecialFunctions.Trigonometric.Inverse"],"declarations":6,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.s5_so3_fiber_action_unconditional","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.s5_so3_fiber_action_unconditional","kind":"theorem","line":89,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidsAndKnots/BringFiberActionInstance.lean#L89-L98","doc":"**`s5_so3_fiber_action_scaffold` is now unconditional** (the `BringFiberAction` hypothesis is\ndischarged by the icosahedral Reeb map): the partition `dim²` sum is `120`, conjugation is involutive,\nand conjugate partitions share a fibre rotation. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.bringFiberAction_icosahedral","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.bringFiberAction_icosahedral","kind":"instance","line":81,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidsAndKnots/BringFiberActionInstance.lean#L81-L87","doc":"**The geometric build: the forced `BringFiberAction` instance.** Each A₅ irrep maps to a rotation\nby its icosahedral Reeb phase `θ_λ = arccos(χ_λ(C₅)/dim_λ)` about the Seifert `S¹` (Reeb) axis. The\nfive phases are distinct (`reebAngle_inj`), discharging `five_distinct_classes` — the content-bearing\ninstance of `conj:s5-so3-fiber-action`, making `s5_so3_fiber_action_scaffold` unconditional. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.reebAngle_inj","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.reebAngle_inj","kind":"theorem","line":72,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidsAndKnots/BringFiberActionInstance.lean#L72-L79","doc":"**The five Reeb phases are distinct** — arccos is injective on `[−1, 1]` and the cosines differ. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.reebCos_inj","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.reebCos_inj","kind":"theorem","line":64,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidsAndKnots/BringFiberActionInstance.lean#L64-L70","doc":"**The five cosines are distinct.** ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.reebAngle","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.reebAngle","kind":"def","line":51,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidsAndKnots/BringFiberActionInstance.lean#L51-L52","doc":"The per-irrep icosahedral Reeb phase `θ_λ = arccos(χ_λ(C₅)/dim_λ)`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.reebCos","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.reebCos","kind":"def","line":43,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidsAndKnots/BringFiberActionInstance.lean#L43-L49","doc":"The forced 5-fold-class cosines `χ_λ(C₅)/dim_λ` of the A₅ character table (PR #2591). ","signatureChunk":0}]}